      "postId": "18106769117015491",
      "text": "A proxy-logging study ( Systima.ai ) found Claude Code sends ~33,000 tokens before you type a word — 27 tools, full scaffolding — versus OpenCode's ~7,000, a 4.7x gap that narrows to 3.3x on Fable 5. Worse: on identical tasks, Claude Code produced up to 54x more cache-write tokens because its prompt prefix isn't byte-stable across turns. Counterintuitively, aggressive tool-call batching can close the total-cost gap on complex multi-step work anyway.",
